+{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01M5pQPxVccyHRu5dqJqURr1","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Phase 10: Recurring Tasks\n2\t\n3\tAdd the ability to schedule tasks that recur on a regular interval using simple cron-like expressions.\n4\t\n5\t## Requirements\n6\t\n7\t- A schedule associates a cron expression with a queue and a task template (the payload to use each time).\n8\t- Support a simple subset of cron expressions:\n9\t  - `*/N * * * *` -- every N minutes\n10\t  - `0 * * * *` -- every hour on the hour\n11\t  - `0 0 * * *` -- every day at midnight\n12\t- There should be a way to create, remove, and list active schedules.\n13\t- A manual \"tick\" or \"check\" mechanism should evaluate all active schedules and enqueue tasks for any that are due. This is used for testing.\n14\t- Once enqueued, recurring tasks are regular tasks subject to all other queue rules.\n15\t- Removing a schedule stops future occurrences from being created.\n16\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"08a9ec0a-0f75-4e4d-a128-e9b53ab70ffc","uuid":"8b8e274b-13ea-48a2-9a78-6f5a0568b12c","timestamp":"2026-05-29T04:25:20.123Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/phases/phase-10.md","content":"# Phase 10: Recurring Tasks\n\nAdd the ability to schedule tasks that recur on a regular interval using simple cron-like expressions.\n\n## Requirements\n\n- A schedule associates a cron expression with a queue and a task template (the payload to use each time).\n- Support a simple subset of cron expressions:\n  - `*/N * * * *` -- every N minutes\n  - `0 * * * *` -- every hour on the hour\n  - `0 0 * * *` -- every day at midnight\n- There should be a way to create, remove, and list active schedules.\n- A manual \"tick\" or \"check\" mechanism should evaluate all active schedules and enqueue tasks for any that are due. This is used for testing.\n- Once enqueued, recurring tasks are regular tasks subject to all other queue rules.\n- Removing a schedule stops future occurrences from being created.\n","numLines":16,"startLine":1,"totalLines":16}}}
+{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TAedzQ2GdbZ5QvmeDdigeh","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Phase 11: Middleware Pipeline\n2\t\n3\tAdd a middleware system that can intercept and transform tasks as they are processed.\n4\t\n5\t## Requirements\n6\t\n7\t- Middleware functions can be registered per queue.\n8\t- When a task is processed, it passes through all registered middleware in order before reaching the final handler.\n9\t- Each middleware receives the task and a \"next\" function. Calling \"next\" passes control to the next middleware (or the handler).\n10\t- If a middleware does NOT call \"next\", the task processing is skipped.\n11\t- Middleware can modify the task (e.g., adding metadata or transforming the payload).\n12\t- If a middleware throws an error, the task should be marked as failed.\n13\t- A processing function/handler can be registered per queue. It is invoked after all middleware have run.\n14\t- Each queue has its own independent middleware stack.\n15\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"08a9ec0a-0f75-4e4d-a128-e9b53ab70ffc","uuid":"67bfa1c2-1918-4e07-825f-d93c146114d0","timestamp":"2026-05-29T04:25:20.124Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/phases/phase-11.md","content":"# Phase 11: Middleware Pipeline\n\nAdd a middleware system that can intercept and transform tasks as they are processed.\n\n## Requirements\n\n- Middleware functions can be registered per queue.\n- When a task is processed, it passes through all registered middleware in order before reaching the final handler.\n- Each middleware receives the task and a \"next\" function. Calling \"next\" passes control to the next middleware (or the handler).\n- If a middleware does NOT call \"next\", the task processing is skipped.\n- Middleware can modify the task (e.g., adding metadata or transforming the payload).\n- If a middleware throws an error, the task should be marked as failed.\n- A processing function/handler can be registered per queue. It is invoked after all middleware have run.\n- Each queue has its own independent middleware stack.\n","numLines":15,"startLine":1,"totalLines":15}}}
