+# CONTRACT — In-Memory Task Queue (12 phases)
+
+Definition of done: every box below behaves as described, `npm run build` compiles,
+and `npm run lint` reports no errors. Tests under `tests/` exercise each behavior.
+
+## Phase 1 — Basic queue
+- [ ] `add(payload)` enqueues a task and returns a `Job` with a unique `id`.
+- [ ] Tasks process one at a time, FIFO, via a registered handler `process((payload, ctx) => ...)`.
+- [ ] Handler receives the task's payload.
+- [ ] Status tracked: `waiting` -> `active` -> `completed`/`failed`.
+- [ ] A handler that throws marks the task `failed`; otherwise `completed`.
+- [ ] `getStatus(id)` / `getTask(id)` returns current status/info by id.
+- [ ] Handler return value is captured as the task result (`job.result()`).
+
+## Phase 2 — Named queues
+- [ ] `TaskQueue.queue(name)` returns an independent queue; same name returns the same instance.
+- [ ] Different queues have independent tasks, handlers, and concurrency.
+
+## Phase 3 — Priority
+- [ ] `add(payload, { priority })`; higher priority runs before lower when both waiting.
+- [ ] Equal priority preserves FIFO order.
+
+## Phase 4 — Delayed tasks
+- [ ] `add(payload, { delay })`; task stays `delayed` and is not picked until the delay elapses.
+- [ ] Delayed tasks become `waiting` automatically when their time arrives.
+
+## Phase 5 — Retry with backoff
+- [ ] `add(payload, { attempts })`; a failing task retries until attempts exhausted.
+- [ ] `backoff` (number | {type: fixed|linear|exponential, delay, factor, maxDelay, jitter}) delays each retry.
+- [ ] `attempt` count is exposed to the handler via `ctx.attempt`.
+- [ ] Task only becomes `failed` after the final attempt fails.
+
+## Phase 6 — Dead letter queue
+- [ ] A task that exhausts its retries is recorded in the dead-letter list.
+- [ ] `deadLetters()` returns those tasks; `'dead-letter'` event fires.
+- [ ] `retry(id)` can requeue a dead/failed task.
+
+## Phase 7 — Dependencies
+- [ ] `add(payload, { dependencies: [ids] })`; task stays `pending` until all deps `completed`.
+- [ ] When the last dependency completes, the dependent becomes eligible.
+- [ ] If a dependency fails/cancels, the dependent fails with a dependency error.
+- [ ] Dependencies declared before the dependency task is added still resolve.
+
+## Phase 8 — Concurrency control
+- [ ] `new Queue(name, { concurrency })` / `setConcurrency(n)` limits simultaneous active tasks.
+- [ ] Default concurrency is 1 (phase 1 FIFO semantics).
+- [ ] At most `concurrency` tasks are `active` at any moment.
+
+## Phase 9 — Progress & cancellation
